+#### 4.9.1 Archived Binance-origin mark events
+
+A Dataset Release MAY use an external archive of the Binance USDⓈ-M `<symbol>@markPrice@1s` WebSocket stream only when every accepted record is an `ARCHIVED_BINANCE_ORIGIN_EVENT`, not merely a `PROVIDER_NORMALIZED_RECORD`. Preserve the original Binance payload bytes and numeric text, Binance event timestamp, provider receive or capture timestamp, and original capture order. Equal exchange timestamps are ordered by preserved capture order. The required target interval MUST contain continuous real captured events in every UTC minute; a provider coverage statement is not target evidence.
+
+Before event-derived minute mark bars can be accepted, the same provider, channel, symbol, parser, ordering rule, and Decimal normalization MUST reproduce official Binance `markPriceKlines` with 100% semantic OHLC agreement over large, multiple known-good control samples inside the Dataset Release window. Use half-open UTC minute boundaries and exact Decimal arithmetic:
+
+``` text
+open = first observed mark event in the minute
+high = exact maximum observed mark price
+low = exact minimum observed mark price
+close = last observed mark event in the minute
+```
+
+Only normalization explicitly justified by the official Instrument price precision is allowed. Interpolation, forward fill, backward fill, nearest value, provider averaging, execution/index/premium/last-price substitution, and synthetic OHLC are forbidden. Prefer agreement between two independent archives for the target interval. One archive MAY suffice only when it supplies exchange-native Binance payloads, proves continuous capture for every target minute, and passes the exact control-validation gate. Any target disagreement or provenance gap remains blocking; no source may be selected silently.
+
+An event-derived result that fails exact control reproduction MUST NOT be called an official mark kline or exported as one. In that case the same real exchange-native events MAY instead be evaluated as event-level Nautilus `MarkPriceUpdate` input only if a pinned-runtime qualification proves exact timestamp, causal availability, valuation, ordering, and replay semantics without creating bars or prices. If that qualification fails or the target events are incomplete, the Dataset Release blocks with `MARK_EVENT_CONTROL_VALIDATION_FAILED` or `MARK_ROLE_INVALID` as applicable.
